// palette.hml — THE MASTER PALETTE. W2-3.
//
// This file IS the look of Nightshade. Every colour the game will ever draw is
// named here, transcribed from `docs/recon/ART_BIBLE.md` §3 (the master
// palette), §5.1 (the time-of-day sky keyframes), §4.4 (emissive window light)
// and §13.7 (the missing-texture tile). Nothing else in `nightshade/src/` may
// contain a hex colour — `tools/ci_imports.sh` greps for it.
//
// PURE DATA. No imports, no engine dependency, no SDL, no allocation at module
// scope. Importing this module costs one constant table and nothing else, which
// is why `src/sim/**` could import it if it ever needed to (it will not).
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE FORMAT
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Every colour is a packed `i32`, `0xRRGGBB`, top byte zero. Positive, so the
// shifts below never touch the sign bit and never trap. This is NOT an SDL
// pixel — SDL's `RGBA32` byte order is handled by whatever writes texels
// (`src/art/texgen.hml`), not here.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE FOUR LAWS THIS TABLE OBEYS (ART_BIBLE §3.1, §2.1, §13.4, CLAUDE.md §8)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  1. NO UNTINTED COLOUR. A colour whose channels are round numbers, or two of
//     whose channels are equal, was typed rather than chosen. `pal_selftest`
//     asserts this over the whole table; there are exactly THREE exemptions and
//     they are named, with reasons, at `pal_is_tint_exempt` below.
//  2. WARM WORLD, COOL SKY, VIOLET THREAT. Terrain/flora/architecture run
//     yellow-green -> ochre -> warm grey. Sky and shadow are cool. The
//     `NS_*` violet family appears ONLY on things hostile, collectable, or
//     player-progression. Guard that harder than any other rule here.
//  3. MINIMUM ALBEDO LUMINANCE 72 in `ATLAS_WORLD`. Vertex colour MULTIPLIES the
//     texture (Rule T1) so a texture can only ever be darkened; author dark and
//     the shadow side becomes an unreadable hole. `pal_selftest` measures this
//     and reports the three ART_BIBLE values that land just under — see the
//     block comment on `pal_is_lum_waived`.
//  4. EVERY FRAME NEEDS A TRUE DARK AND A TRUE LIGHT (below luminance 30, above
//     220). The table must be able to supply both.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// VERIFY
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//     hemlockc --check src/art/palette.hml
//     hemlockc -O1 tools/probe_palette.hml -o /tmp/probe_palette && /tmp/probe_palette
//
// `pal_selftest()` lives in this file (W2-3 owns only this file) and the probe
// is a four-line driver around it.

