// ===========================================================================
// ART_BIBLE §5.1 — THE TIME-OF-DAY SKY KEYFRAMES
//
// The seven keyframes of the day/night cycle each override the five sky/cloud
// colours above. They live here, not in `src/art/tod.hml`, for one reason: no
// colour is hardcoded outside this file, ever. `tod.hml` (W2-4) indexes these
// by keyframe and `pal_lerp`s between them; `skygen.hml` (W2-6) bakes them.
//
// The table is deliberately uniform — all seven keyframes present for all five
// rows, including NOON, whose values are identical to the unsuffixed §3.2
// constants above (asserted by `pal_selftest`). A caller can therefore index
// keyframe 0..6 without a special case, which is worth five duplicated
// literals.
//
// `CLOUD_MID` has no per-keyframe row in the ART_BIBLE; derive it as
// `pal_lerp(g_CLOUD_SHADOW_<KF>, g_CLOUD_LIT_<KF>, 0.5)`-ish, per §11.2.
// ===========================================================================

